  ],
  "analysis": [
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "answer": "Under current law, the state personal income tax rate is 5 percent. The measure increases this rate to 6 percent for taxable years starting on or after January 1, 2028.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "answer": "The direct cost is the additional 1 percent of taxable income that taxpayers will owe to the state. The opportunity cost includes reduced disposable income that individuals could have otherwise used for private consumption, savings, or investment.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "answer": "Individuals and families with taxable income pay the higher tax rate. The state government, along with the programs, contractors, and public employees funded by state revenues, benefits from the increased tax collections.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "answer": "Taxpayers may adjust their behavior to minimize their tax burden by increasing tax-deductible contributions, deferring income, or, in some cases, relocating to jurisdictions with lower tax rates. The state government will likely adjust its future budgets to account for higher projected revenues.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "answer": "The text does not explicitly assert a problem. The mechanism addresses state funding by extracting a larger share of personal income to support the general fund or state spending.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q7",
      "answer": "Researchers disagree on the net effect of broad-based income tax increases on jobs and investment. Some research finds that higher income taxes reduce private sector investment, entrepreneurial activity, and hiring by lowering after-tax returns on labor and capital. Other research finds that if the resulting revenue is deployed toward productive public investments, such as education or infrastructure, the net economic effect can be neutral or positive.",
      "disputed": true
    }
  ],
